\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\f0\fs20 Tower Version 15.50x64    9:12:22 a.m. Monday, 24 June 2019\par
Beca Ltd - New Zealand\par
\par
\pard\qj\lang1033 Tower Type: \tab Tower Type TD - Modelled by Elsie De Vera, BECA \par
\pard\fi720\li1440\qj Reviewed by Ben Evans, Senior Transmission Line Engineer, BECA\par
October 2019\par
\pard\qj\par
Construction Date:\tab\par
\par
Drawings date:\tab 1959\par
\par
Drawings used:\tab 330kV Single Line Sydney South - Sydney North Type TD Tower\par
\tab\tab\tab TL-049068 (P13136) - UPPER SUPERSTRUCTURE\par
\tab\tab\tab TL-049067 (P13137) - SUPERSTRUCTURE\par
\tab\tab\tab TL-049066 (T1949) - LEG EXTENSION\par
\tab\tab\tab TL-049062 (T1992) - 26'3" LEG EXTENSION\par
\tab\tab\tab TL-049063 (T2034) - 36'3" LEG EXTENSION\par
\tab\tab\tab TL-033817 (P33817) - ULTIMATE DESIGN LOADS TENSION TYPE TD ANGLE POSITION\par
\tab\tab\tab TL-033819 ONLY A PORTION (LOADS TABLE) OF THE DRAWING CAN BE SEEN IN THE EDMS-TL FILE\tab\tab\tab\tab\tab\tab\tab\par
\tab\tab\tab\par
\pard\fi-2160\li2160\qj Steel Material: \tab Mild and High Tensile Steel chosen from standards of similar era of drawings \par
\pard\qj\par
\pard\fi-2160\li2160\qj Bolts:\tab High Tensile Steel Bolts \par
\pard\qj\par
Modelling Notes and Assumptions:\par
\par
\pard TransGrid require tower models to be developed for existing towers to be able to carry out a full structural analysis.\par
BECA Job Number for this project: 2589168 - Tower Modelling - TL24\par
 \par
\pard\fi-720\li1080\qj 1.\tab Guidance for structure design/modelling is taken from TL-A-03 PLS Pole and Tower Modelling Guideline_0.1A\par
2.\tab Steel to BS15:1936/48/61 for Mild Steel (247 MPa Yield strength)and BS968:1962 for High Tensile Steel (340 MPa Yield strength).\par
3.\tab Bolts M14 in 15.5mm dia. hole, M16 in 17.5mm dia. hole, M20 in 21.5mm dia. hole, M22 in 23.5mm dia. hole, M24 in 25.5mm dia. hole, M27 in 29mm dia. hole,  5/8\rdblquote  in 11/16\rdblquote  diameter hole, 3/4\rdblquote  in 13/16\rdblquote  diameter hole, 7/8\rdblquote  in 15/16\rdblquote , 1\rdblquote  in 1 1/16\rdblquote  hole and 1 1/8\rdblquote  in 1 3/16\rdblquote  diameter hole. Bolts library taken from existing TransGrid library file.\par
4.\tab Sections sizes are taken from referenced drawings. Section properties are taken from existing TransGrid library file.\par
5.\tab Approach to modelling TransGrid towers is based on \ldblquote simplistic\rdblquote  approach, legs and crossarms to gauge lines.\par
6.\tab Insulator attachments nodes are modelled; maintenance holes are not modelled.\par
7.\tab Panel heights are interpreted from gauge lines.\par
8.\tab Connection block shear is not calculated.\par
\lang3081 9.\tab Drag factors are calculated as per the original design pressure shown on TL-033817 and TL-033819.\par
10.On the longitudinal face of the superstructure crossing diagonals have not been used in some cases due to a third member requiring a node in the middle. The members have not been modelled conservatively to not account for any restraint from another crossing member.  If this fails, a check to determine whether it is appropriate to assume crossing diagonal action can be applied for all load cases is required.\par
11.For Leg panel members with braces in both faces, a 1.2 effective length factor is included when there are more than three nodes between positions of equal restraint in both faces.\par
\pard\fi-720\li1080\sa200\sl276\slmult1 12.Analysis type is linear as per TransGrid advice.\par
13.Common design practice is to design redundant members for 1 to 2.5% of the load in the supported members in accordance with C3.7.4 ASCE 10-97. \par
14. Body and leg extensions are included in the model.  See Family Manager.\par
\par
\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1 2023/04/28\line RP3 TL23 LINE REFURBISHMENT\line APD ENGINEERING\par
Updates:\par
   1. Updated crossarm face and plan bracing arrangement to TL-049068\line    2. Updated bridge face and plan bracing arrangement to TL-049068\line    3. Updated body to TL-049067 basic body and TL-061026 body ext\line    4. Updated leg extension to TL-049066 +18'-9" leg\par
\par
\pard\lang5129\par
